<p>
<a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/10/upcoming-chat-with-linkarzu-about-using-emacs-for-25-years/">While summarizing my history with Emacs</a>, I was curious about just how many <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/category/emacs-news">Emacs News</a> posts I've written and how many links I've highlighted. 564 posts, &gt; 34000 items, an average of 60 items per posts.
</p>

<p>
Analysis: It turned out that my <a href="https://github.com/sachac/emacs-news">emacs-news/index.org</a> only went back to about 2016,
missing a few months of 2015.
To fill in the data, I needed to convert the old HTML files into Org format.
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-:eval"><code>find -name \*news\*.html -exec zsh -c 'pandoc -f html -t org {} &#45;&#45;wrap=none -o $(basename {} .html).org' \;
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
Then I inserted the old entries into my file.
<code>insert-file-contents</code> doesn't seem to move the point, but if I narrow to my Posts subtree (<code>org-narrow-to-subtree</code>), then I can go to the end of the narrowed part.
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-emacs-news-insert-old-ones</span> ()
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((dir <span class="org-string">"~/proj/static-blog/blog/2015/"</span>))
    (<span class="org-keyword">dolist</span> (f
             (sort
              (directory-files-recursively dir <span class="org-string">"news.*org$"</span>)
              <span class="org-builtin">:key</span> <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">#'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">file-name-base</span>
              <span class="org-builtin">:reverse</span> t))
      (insert <span class="org-string">"** "</span> (substring (file-name-base f) 0 10) <span class="org-string">" Emacs News\n\n"</span>)
      (insert-file-contents f)
      (goto-char (point-max)))))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
With all the entries in place, let's look at the list items that start with a link.
</p>

<details><summary>code for analysis</summary>
<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code><span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-emacs-news-count-links</span> ()
  <span class="org-doc">"Return the number of main links in this subtree."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((count 0))
    (<span class="org-keyword">save-excursion</span>
      (org-back-to-heading)
      (<span class="org-keyword">while</span> (re-search-forward <span class="org-string">"^ *- \\[\\["</span> (<span class="org-keyword">save-excursion</span> (org-end-of-subtree)) t)
        (<span class="org-keyword">incf</span> count)))
    (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (called-interactively-p <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">any</span>)
      (message <span class="org-string">"%d"</span> count))
    count))

<span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-emacs-news-analyze</span> ()
  <span class="org-doc">"Count how many entries and items. Make a table of entries."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">with-current-buffer</span> (find-file-noselect <span class="org-string">"~/sync/emacs-news/index.org"</span>)
    (goto-char (point-min))
    (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> (results)
      (org-map-entries
       (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> ()
         (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((title (org-entry-get (point) <span class="org-string">"ITEM"</span>)))
           (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (string-match <span class="org-string">"</span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-backslash">\\</span></span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-construct">(</span></span><span class="org-string">[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]</span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-backslash">\\</span></span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-construct">)</span></span><span class="org-string"> Emacs"</span> title)
             (<span class="org-keyword">push</span> (list (match-string 1 title)
                         (sacha-emacs-news-count-links))
                   results)))))
      (seq-uniq (sort results <span class="org-builtin">:key</span> <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">car</span> <span class="org-builtin">:reverse</span> t)))))
</code></pre>
</div>

</details>


